{"text": "To achieve the target number 24 using the numbers [1, 2, 5, 7] exactly once with the operations +, -, *, and /, we can follow this solution:", "start": 0, "end": 140, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "We start by considering a combination that leads to 24.", "start": 142, "end": 197, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "One effective way is to use the multiplication and division operations to get close to 24.", "start": 198, "end": 288, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Here's a step-by-step breakdown of a possible solution:", "start": 289, "end": 344, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "1. Start by multiplying 5 and 4:", "start": 346, "end": 378, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "5 × 4 = 20", "start": 380, "end": 390, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "2. Now, we need to get 4 using the remaining numbers 1 and 7.", "start": 392, "end": 453, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Notice that:", "start": 454, "end": 466, "label": "inform"}
